msgstr "**Fig 2** (TODO : INSERT PHOTO, apple harvest)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:24
msgid "Apples and crabapples"
msgstr "Pommes et pommettes"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:26
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:102
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:172
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:266
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:344
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:418
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:494
msgid "Harvest period"
msgstr "Période de récolte"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:27
msgid ""
"In Montréal, the apple and crabapple season generally runs from late "
"August to October."
msgstr ""
"À Montréal, la saison des pommes et des pommettes s’étend généralement de"
" la fin août à octobre."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:29
msgid "Early apples: mid-July to mid-August"
msgstr "Pommes hâtives : mi-juillet à mi-août"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:30
msgid "Mid-season apples: September to October"
msgstr "Pommes de saison : septembre à octobre"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:31
msgid "Crabapples: mid-August to mid-September"
msgstr "Pommettes (crabapples) : mi-août à mi-septembre"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:33
msgid ""
"Maturity varies considerably depending on the cultivar and the urban "
"micro-site."
msgstr ""
"La maturité varie fortement selon les cultivars et les micro-sites "
"urbains."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:35
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:107
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:178
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:272
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:348
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:423
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:501
msgid "How to recognize the right stage of maturity"
msgstr "Comment reconnaître le bon moment de maturité"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:37
msgid "**Apples**"
msgstr "**Pommes**"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:38
msgid "Colour has developed according to the cultivar."
msgstr "Couleur développée selon le cultivar."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:39
msgid "The fruit is firm but detaches easily when lifted."
msgstr "Fruit ferme mais qui se détache facilement en le soulevant."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:40
msgid "The flavour has a good balance of sweetness and acidity."
msgstr "Goût sucré/acidulé équilibré."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:41
msgid "The seeds are dark brown, which is an indicator of internal maturity."
msgstr "Les pépins sont de couleur brun foncé (indice de maturité interne)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:43
msgid "**Crabapples**"
msgstr "**Pommettes**"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:44
msgid "Bright colour (red, yellow, or orange, depending on the variety)."
msgstr "Couleur vive (rouge, jaune, orange selon variété)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:45
msgid "Fruit is slightly soft."
msgstr "Fruits légèrement souples."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:46
msgid "Fruit remains attached to the tree, but maturity is often uneven."
msgstr "Bonne tenue sur l’arbre, mais maturité souvent irrégulière."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:48
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:119
msgid "**Leave on the tree:**"
msgstr "**À laisser sur l’arbre :**"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:49
msgid "Very green, hard fruit."
msgstr "Fruits très verts et durs."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:50
msgid "Immature fruit with a very astringent taste."
msgstr "Fruits immatures avec goût très astringent."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:52
msgid ""
"**Remember:** Not all fruit on the same tree ripens at the same time. You"
" may need to visit a tree several times over one to two weeks as the "
"fruit matures, so you can harvest at the right time."
msgstr ""
"**à retenir :** tous les fruits d’un même arbre ne mûrissent pas toujours"
" en même temps. Il faut parfois visiter un arbre plusieurs fois pendant "
"les 1 à 2 semaines de sa période de maturité pour intervenir au bon "
"moment."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:54
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:126
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:206
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:288
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:371
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:443
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:522
msgid "Harvesting techniques"
msgstr "Techniques de cueillette"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:56
msgid ""
"Apples should be picked with a twisting motion accompanied by a gentle "
"lift; ideally, by pressing on the stem with the tip of your finger to "
"ensure that the spur does not tear as the fruit detaches. If the fruit "
"does not come off easily, it is not ripe. By hand: Turn the apple while "
"slightly raising and pull gently. Do not pull down on the fruit.  With "
"fruit picking tool: position the metal part around the apple, lift "
"slightly and rotate (see Fig 2). Do not pull down on the fruit."
msgstr ""
"Les pommes doivent être cueillies d’un geste de rotation accompagné d’un "
"léger soulèvement ; idéalement, en appuyant sur la tige avec la pousse "
"pour assurer que la coursonne ne se déchire pas en même temps que le "
"fruit se détache. Si le fruit ne se détache pas facilement, c’est qu’il "
"n’est pas mûr."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:59
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:131
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:295
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:375
msgid "Pick by hand, one fruit at a time."
msgstr "Cueillir à la main, fruit par fruit."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:60
msgid "Lift and twist slightly to detach the fruit; avoid pulling."
msgstr "Soulever et tourner légèrement pour détacher (éviter de tirer)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:61
msgid ""
"Ideally, do not shake the branches, as this can cause immature fruit to "
"fall and injure the tree."
msgstr ""
"Idéalement, ne pas secouer les branches (risque de chute de fruits "
"immatures et blessures à l’arbre)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:62
msgid "Prioritize accessible, ripe fruit, making several passes if needed."
msgstr "Prioriser les fruits accessibles et mûrs en plusieurs passages."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:64
msgid "**For tall trees:**"
msgstr "**Pour arbres hauts :**"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:65
msgid "Use a safe step ladder or suitable picking poles."
msgstr "Utiliser escabeau sécuritaire ou perches de cueillette adaptées"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:66
msgid "Always secure the area beneath the tree."
msgstr "Toujours sécuriser la zone sous l’arbre."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:68
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:140
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:220
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:304
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:384
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:452
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:533
msgid "Sorting"
msgstr "Triage"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:70
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:141
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:222
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:306
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:386
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:455
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:534
msgid "Keep:"
msgstr "Conserver :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:71
msgid "Firm, intact fruit."
msgstr "Fruits fermes et intacts."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:72
msgid "Fruit without punctures or cracks."
msgstr "Fruits sans perforations ni fissures."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:73
msgid "Fruit without soft spots."
msgstr "Fruits sans zones molles."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:75
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:146
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:227
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:311
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:391
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:458
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:539
msgid "Discard:"
msgstr "Écarter :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:76
msgid "Fruit that has fallen to the ground and is damaged."
msgstr "Fruits tombés au sol et abîmés."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:77
msgid "Soft, rotten, damaged, or fermented fruit."
msgstr "Fruits mous, pourries, abîmés ou fermentés."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:78
msgid "Fruit with insect punctures."
msgstr "Fruits perforés (insectes)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:79
msgid "Fruit with extensive spotting and internal deterioration."
msgstr "Fruits très tachés avec dégradation interne."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:81
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:152
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:235
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:317
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:397
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:466
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:545
msgid "Transport and storage"
msgstr "Transport et entreposage"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:82
msgid ""
"Apples and crabapples are relatively sturdy but sensitive to internal "
"bruising. Do not handle apples like potatoes: they bruise easily, so "
"place them down gently and empty containers carefully."
msgstr ""
"Les pommes et pommettes sont relativement robustes mais sensibles aux "
"chocs internes. Il ne faut pas traiter les pommes comme des patates : "
"elles s’abîment très facilement. Il faut donc les déposer doucement et "
"transvider les bacs avec soin."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:84
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:156
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:239
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:321
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:400
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:548
msgid "Recommended:"
msgstr "Recommandé :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:85
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:322
msgid "Shallow, rigid containers"
msgstr "Contenants rigides peu profonds"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:86
msgid "A single layer, if possible"
msgstr "Une seule couche si possible"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:87
msgid "Gentle handling"
msgstr "Manipulation douce"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:88
msgid "Prompt refrigeration (ideally between 4 and 10 degrees)"
msgstr "Réfrigération rapide (température entre 4 et 10 degrés idéalement)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:90
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:166
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:250
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:330
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:554
msgid "Storage life"
msgstr "Conservation :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:91
msgid ""
"Several weeks or even months in a cool place, depending on cultivar and "
"maturity."
msgstr "Plusieurs semaines, voire mois, au frais (selon cultivar et maturité)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:92
msgid "Crabapples sometimes keep well for only a few weeks."
msgstr "Pommettes : parfois meilleure tenue sur quelques semaines seulement"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:94
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:335
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:410
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:484
msgid "Distribution notes"
msgstr "Notes pour la distribution"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:95
msgid "Good potential for storage and gradual redistribution."
msgstr "Très bon potentiel de stockage et redistribution progressive."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:96
msgid "Apples are ideal for distribution over several weeks."
msgstr "Pommes idéales pour distribution sur plusieurs semaines."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:97
msgid "Crabapples are often best used in processed products (jellies, syrups)."
msgstr "Pommettes souvent mieux valorisées en transformation (gelées, sirops)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:98
msgid ""
"They are sensitive to impacts, so sorting and careful handling are "
"important."
msgstr "Sensibles aux chocs → tri et manipulation importants."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:100
msgid "Cherries"
msgstr "Cerises"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:103
msgid ""
"In Montréal, cherry trees generally produce fruit from late June to mid-"
"July."
msgstr ""
"À Montréal, les cerisiers produisent généralement de la fin juin à la mi-"
"juillet."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:105
msgid ""
"The harvest window is short and depends heavily on sun exposure. Fruit "
"can go from unripe to overripe within a few days. Cherries do not ripen "
"after picking, so they must be harvested when fully ripe."
msgstr ""
"La période de récolte est courte et dépend fortement de l’exposition au "
"soleil. Les fruits peuvent passer de non mûrs à surmûris en quelques "
"jours. Les cerises ne mûrissent pas après la cueillette : elles doivent "
"être récoltées pleinement mûres."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:109
msgid "**Sweet cherries**"
msgstr "**Cerises sucrées (douces)**"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:110
msgid "Dark red to almost black, depending on the variety"
msgstr "Rouge foncé à presque noir selon la variété"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:111
msgid "Shiny, firm but slightly yielding"
msgstr "Fruits brillants et fermes mais souples"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:112
msgid "Clearly sweet, without strong acidity"
msgstr "Goût bien sucré, sans acidité forte"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:114
msgid "**Sour cherries**"
msgstr "**Griottes**"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:115
msgid "Bright red to dark red"
msgstr "Rouge vif à rouge foncé"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:116
msgid "More acidic flavour, even when ripe"
msgstr "Saveur plus acide, même à maturité"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:117
msgid "Fully coloured throughout the fruit"
msgstr "Fruits bien colorés sur tout leur volume"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:120
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:430
msgid "Green fruit"
msgstr "Fruits verts"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:121
msgid "Partially coloured fruit (pale pink or yellow-red)"
msgstr "Fruits partiellement colorés (rose clair, jaune-rouge)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:122
msgid "Fruit that is still firm and acidic"
msgstr "Fruits encore fermes et acides"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:124
msgid ""
"Cherries must be harvested as soon as they reach optimum ripeness: "
"waiting until they are overripe significantly increases the risk of the "
"fruit becoming mushy and of fruit flies or their larvae being present. As"
" soon as the fruit begins to ripen, you must take action to harvest at "
"the optimum time."
msgstr ""
"Les cerises doivent être récoltées dès maturité optimale : attendre la "
"surmaturité augmente fortement le risque de fruits ramollis et de "
"présence de drosophiles (mouches des fruits) ou de larves. Dès le moment "
"où les fruits commencent à mûrir, il faut agir pour intervenir au moment "
"optimal."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:128
msgid ""
"Always pick cherries with the stem intact; otherwise, they will spoil "
"quickly!"
msgstr ""
"Cueillez toujours les cerises avec la tige intacte sinon elles se "
"gâteront rapidement !"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:130
msgid ""
"By hand: Hold the fruit at the end of the stem. Twist it, or gently pull "
"it sideways or upward until the joint at the end of the stem separates "
"from the branch. Do not pull the stem downward. Do not use scissors to "
"cut the stem."
msgstr ""
"À la main : Saisissez le fruit à l’extrémité de la tige. Ensuite soit "
"tournez ou tirez doucement sur un côté ou vers le haut, jusqu’à ce que le"
" nœud à l’extrémité de la tige se défasse de la branche. Ne tirez pas la "
"tige vers le bas. N’utilisez pas de ciseaux pour couper la tige."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:132
msgid ""
"Keep the stem attached to avoid damaging the flesh and to extend "
"potential storage life."
msgstr ""
"Prendre le fruit avec son pédoncule pour éviter d’abîmer la chair et "
"prolonger son temps d’entreposage potentiel."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:133
msgid "Avoid pulling on branches, which are fragile."
msgstr "Éviter de tirer sur les branches (fragiles)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:134
msgid "Make several passes during the season."
msgstr "Effectuer plusieurs passages pendant la saison."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:136
msgid "For high branches:"
msgstr "Pour les branches hautes :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:137
msgid "Use a secure step ladder or suitable picking poles, if available."
msgstr "Utiliser un escabeau sécurisé ou des perches adaptées si disponibles."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:138
msgid "Prioritize safety during harvesting."
msgstr "Prioriser la sécurité avant la récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:142
msgid "Well-coloured, firm fruit"
msgstr "Fruits bien colorés et fermes"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:143
msgid "Fruit without cracks or injuries"
msgstr "Fruits sans fissures ni blessures"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:144
msgid "Fruit that is dry to the touch"
msgstr "Fruits secs au toucher"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:147
msgid "Green or partially ripe fruit"
msgstr "Fruits verts ou partiellement mûrs"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:148
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:313
msgid "Split fruit (after rain)"
msgstr "Fruits éclatés (après pluie)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:149
msgid "Soft, fermented, or mouldy fruit"
msgstr "Fruits mous, fermentés ou moisissures"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:150
msgid "Fruit badly damaged by birds"
msgstr "Fruits très abîmés par les oiseaux"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:154
msgid "Cherries are fragile and easily crushed."
msgstr "Les cerises sont fragiles et sensibles à l’écrasement."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:157
msgid "Small, shallow, rigid containers"
msgstr "Petits contenants rigides peu profonds"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:158
msgid "Very shallow layers of fruit"
msgstr "Récolte en couches minimes"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:159
msgid "Prompt refrigeration after picking"
msgstr "Réfrigération rapide après cueillette"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:161
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:245
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:326
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:473
msgid "**Avoid:**"
msgstr "**À éviter :**"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:162
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:246
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:327
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:474
msgid "Soft bags"
msgstr "Sacs souples"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:163
msgid "Piling fruit"
msgstr "Empilement de fruits"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:164
msgid "Prolonged exposure to heat"
msgstr "Exposition prolongée à la chaleur"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:167
msgid "2–5 days in the refrigerator"
msgstr "2 à 5 jours au réfrigérateur"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:168
msgid "Freezing is possible; pitting them first is ideal"
msgstr "Congélation possible (dénoyautées idéalement)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:170
msgid "Mulberries"
msgstr "Mûrier"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:174
msgid ""
"In Montréal, mulberries generally ripen from early July to mid-August, "
"depending on the species, sun exposure, and weather."
msgstr ""
"À Montréal, les mûres du mûrier arrivent généralement à maturité entre le"
" début juillet et la mi-août, selon l’espèce, l’exposition au soleil et "
"les conditions météorologiques."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:176
msgid ""
"Unlike many other tree fruits, the harvest can extend over several weeks "
"because fruit on the same tree does not ripen all at once. Several visits"
" per week may be needed during this period to pick fruit at its best."
msgstr ""
"Contrairement à plusieurs autres fruits arboricoles, la période de "
"récolte peut s’échelonner sur plusieurs semaines puisque les fruits d’un "
"même arbre ne mûrissent pas tous simultanément. Plusieurs visites par "
"semaine durant cette période sont souvent nécessaires pour récolter les "
"fruits à leur meilleur."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:180
msgid ""
"Mulberries are ready to pick when they reach their mature colour and "
"detach easily from their stems. They start to fall as soon as they are "
"ripe."
msgstr ""
"Les mûres sont prêtes à être récoltées lorsqu’elles atteignent leur "
"couleur mature et se détachent facilement de leur pédoncule. Elles "
"commencent à tomber dès la maturité."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:182
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:276
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:352
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:424
msgid "Ready to pick"
msgstr "Prêtes à cueillir :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:183
msgid "Black, dark purple, or dark red fruit, depending on the variety."
msgstr "Fruits noirs, violet foncé ou rouge foncé selon la variété"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:184
msgid "Soft and juicy fruit."
msgstr "Fruits souples et juteux"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:185
msgid "Fruit that detaches easily to the touch."
msgstr "Fruits qui se détachent facilement au toucher"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:187
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:282
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:358
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:429
msgid "**Leave on the tree**"
msgstr "**À laisser sur l’arbre :**"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:188
msgid "Green fruit."
msgstr "Fruits verts."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:189
msgid "White or pink fruit (for dark-fruited varieties)."
msgstr "Fruits blancs ou rosés (pour les variétés foncées)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:190
msgid "Firm fruit that is difficult to detach."
msgstr "Fruits fermes et difficiles à détacher."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:192
msgid ""
"Mulberries do not continue to ripen significantly after picking, so it is"
" important to harvest them when fully ripe."
msgstr ""
"Les mûres ne continuent pas à mûrir de façon significative après la "
"récolte. Il est donc important de les cueillir à pleine maturité."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:194
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:363
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:436
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:515
msgid "Species-specific characteristics"
msgstr "Particularités de l’espèce"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:196
msgid ""
"Mulberry trees can be especially productive and may yield very large "
"quantities of fruit."
msgstr ""
"Les mûriers sont des arbres particulièrement généreux pouvant produire de"
" très grandes quantités de fruits."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:198
msgid ""
"Ripe fruit falls easily to the ground, which can make for abundant but "
"short-lived harvests. Beneath some trees, the ground can quickly become "
"covered with fallen fruit."
msgstr ""
"Les fruits mûrs tombent facilement au sol, ce qui peut rendre les "
"récoltes abondantes mais de courte durée. Sous certains arbres, le sol "
"peut rapidement se couvrir de fruits tombés."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:200
msgid ""
"Mulberries naturally fall as soon as they reach full maturity. A "
"significant proportion of the crop can therefore end up on the ground "
"within just a few days, especially after wind or rain."
msgstr ""
"Les mûres tombent naturellement dès qu’elles atteignent leur pleine "
"maturité. Une proportion importante de la récolte peut donc se retrouver "
"au sol en quelques jours seulement, particulièrement après des épisodes "
"de vent ou de pluie."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:202
msgid ""
"Birds are very fond of mulberries and may consume a large part of the "
"crop."
msgstr ""
"Les mûres sont très appréciées par les oiseaux, qui peuvent consommer une"
" part importante de la récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:204
msgid ""
"The fruit stains hands, clothing, and surfaces heavily. Wear clothes that"
" you do not mind staining during harvesting activities."
msgstr ""
"Les fruits tachent fortement les mains, les vêtements et les surfaces. Il"
" est recommandé de porter des vêtements qui ne craignent pas les taches "
"lors des activités de récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:208
msgid ""
"Mulberries can be picked by hand when they are within easy reach, but "
"this method is generally inefficient for tall trees."
msgstr ""
"Les mûres peuvent être récoltées à la main lorsqu’elles sont facilement "
"accessibles, mais cette méthode est généralement peu efficace pour les "
"arbres de grande taille."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:210
msgid "For large trees, a commonly used method is to:"
msgstr "Pour les grands arbres, une méthode couramment utilisée consiste à :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:211
msgid "Spread or hold a clean tarp beneath one main branch at a time."
msgstr "Étendre ou tenir une bâche propre sous une charpentière à la fois."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:212
msgid "Gently shake the branch so ripe fruit falls onto the tarp."
msgstr ""
"Secouer doucement la branche afin de faire tomber les fruits mûrs sur la "
"bâche."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:213
msgid "Move the tarp to another main branch and repeat."
msgstr ""
"Déplacer ensuite la bâche vers une autre charpentière et répéter "
"l’opération."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:214
msgid "Collect the fruit that has fallen onto the tarp."
msgstr "Ramasser les fruits tombés sur la bâche."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:216
msgid ""
"This technique makes it possible to harvest large quantities efficiently "
"while limiting handling."
msgstr ""
"Cette technique permet de récolter efficacement de grandes quantités de "
"fruits tout en limitant les manipulations."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:218
msgid "Avoid shaking branches too vigorously, so that unripe fruit does not fall."
msgstr ""
"Éviter de secouer excessivement les branches afin de ne pas faire tomber "
"les fruits encore immatures."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:223
msgid "Fully ripe fruit."
msgstr "Fruits bien mûrs"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:224
msgid "Fruit that is still firm despite being ripe."
msgstr "Fruits fermes malgré leur maturité"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:225
msgid "Clean, intact fruit."
msgstr "Fruits propres et intacts"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:228
msgid "Green or insufficiently ripe fruit."
msgstr "Fruits verts ou insuffisamment mûrs"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:229
msgid "Dried-out fruit."
msgstr "Fruits desséchés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:230
msgid "Fruit showing mould."
msgstr "Fruits présentant de la moisissure"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:231
msgid "Crushed or fermenting fruit."
msgstr "Fruits écrasés ou en fermentation"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:233
msgid ""
"When harvesting with a tarp, remove leaves, twigs, and other plant debris"
" before storage."
msgstr ""
"Lorsque la récolte est réalisée à l’aide d’une bâche, retirer les "
"feuilles, brindilles et autres débris végétaux avant l’entreposage"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:237
msgid "Mulberries are fragile and do not keep for long after picking."
msgstr ""
"Les mûres du mûrier sont des fruits fragiles qui se conservent peu "
"longtemps après la récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:240
msgid "Use shallow containers."
msgstr "Utiliser des contenants peu profonds."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:241
msgid ""
"Prefer small, rigid, reused containers such as those used for "
"strawberries, raspberries, or blueberries."
msgstr ""
"Privilégier de petites barquettes rigides réutilisées, comme celles "
"utilisées pour les fraises, framboises ou bleuets."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:242
msgid "Avoid crushing the fruit under its own weight."
msgstr "Éviter d’écraser les fruits sous leur propre poids."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:243
msgid "Refrigerate promptly after harvesting."
msgstr "Réfrigérer rapidement après la récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:247
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:475
msgid "Containers that are too deep"
msgstr "Les contenants trop profonds"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:248
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:476
msgid "Excessive stacking of fruit"
msgstr "Les empilements excessifs de fruits"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:251
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:331
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:555
msgid "A few days in the refrigerator."
msgstr "Quelques jours au réfrigérateur."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:252
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:332
msgid "Freezing is possible."
msgstr "Congélation possible."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:253
msgid "Prompt processing is recommended for large harvests."
msgstr "Transformation rapide recommandée pour les grandes récoltes."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:255
msgid "Mulberries are popular, but their storage life is limited."
msgstr ""
"Les mûres sont très appréciées, mais leur durée de conservation est "
"limitée."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:257
msgid "It is recommended that you:"
msgstr "Il est recommandé de :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:258
msgid "Distribute them quickly after harvesting."
msgstr "Distribuer rapidement après la récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:259
msgid "Avoid excessive handling."
msgstr "Éviter les manipulations excessives."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:260
msgid ""
"Tell recipients that the fruit should be eaten or processed quickly. "
"Mulberries are particularly well suited to community kitchens, community "
"fridges, and food-processing initiatives."
msgstr ""
"Informer les bénéficiaires de la nécessité de consommer ou de transformer"
" les fruits rapidement. Ou bien les congeler pour utilisation plus tard. "
"Les mûres sont donc particulièrement bien adaptées aux cuisines "
"collectives, aux frigos communautaires et aux initiatives de "
"transformation alimentaire."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:262
msgid ""
"Large harvests are especially suitable for group processing (jams, "
"jellies, and freezing)."
msgstr ""
"Les récoltes abondantes se prêtent particulièrement bien à la "
"transformation collective (confitures, gelées, congélation)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:264
msgid "Plums"
msgstr "Prunes"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:268
msgid ""
"In Montréal, the plum season is long, generally running from mid-July "
"(e.g., ‘Early Golden’) to late October (e.g., ‘Mont-Royal’). However, "
"most plum trees are ready for harvest in August."
msgstr ""
"À Montréal, la saison des prunes est longue : elle s’étend généralement "
"de la mi-juillet (ex. : ‘Early Golden’) à la fin octobre (ex. : ‘Mont-"
"Royal’). Toutefois, la majorité des pruniers sont prêts en août."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:270
msgid ""
"Ripening progresses differently depending on the cultivar and site. Some "
"trees may therefore be ready for harvest over several weeks, with "
"different peak periods for different varieties."
msgstr ""
"La maturation est progressive selon les cultivars et les sites. Il peut "
"donc y avoir des arbres en pleine récolte pendant plusieurs semaines, "
"avec des pics différents selon les variétés."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:274
msgid ""
"Plums should be picked when fully ripe; they do not ripen significantly "
"after picking."
msgstr ""
"Les prunes doivent être récoltées à pleine maturité ; elles ne mûrissent "
"pas significativement après la cueillette."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:277
msgid "The colour typical of the cultivar (yellow, red, purple, or dark blue)"
msgstr "Couleur typique du cultivar (jaune, rouge, violet, bleu foncé)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:278
msgid "Fruit that is slightly soft to the touch"
msgstr "Fruit légèrement souple au toucher"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:279
msgid "Fruit that detaches easily from the branch (for some cultivars)"
msgstr "Détachement facile de la branche (certains cultivars)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:280
msgid ""
"A developed sweet flavour, or a balanced sweet-acid flavour depending on "
"the variety"
msgstr "Saveur sucrée développée (ou équilibrée acide/sucré selon variété)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:283
msgid "Green or very firm fruit"
msgstr "Fruits verts ou très fermes"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:284
msgid "Fruit that is still acidic and not very colourful"
msgstr "Fruits encore acides et peu colorés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:286
msgid ""
"Overripe fruit softens quickly, and the risk of spotted-wing drosophila "
"(fruit flies) increases. This can lead to internal deterioration and the "
"presence of larvae."
msgstr ""
"La surmaturité augmente rapidement le ramollissement et le risque de "
"drosophiles (mouches des fruits), pouvant entraîner dégradation interne "
"et présence de larves."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:290
msgid ""
"Plums can be picked in the same way as apples. A ripe plum detaches "
"easily."
msgstr ""
"Les prunes peuvent être cueillies de la même manière que les pommes. Une "
"prune mûre se détache facilement."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:292
msgid "By hand: Gently turn the plum upward. Do not pull the fruit downward."
msgstr ""
"À la main : Tournez la prune délicatement vers le haut. Ne tirez pas le "
"fruit vers le bas."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:294
msgid ""
"With a fruit picker: Position the metal part around the plum, lift "
"gently, and twist. Do not pull the fruit downward."
msgstr ""
"Avec un cueille-fruits : Positionnez la partie métallique autour de la "
"prune, soulevez doucement et tournez. Ne tirez pas le fruit vers le bas."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:296
msgid "Twist the fruit slightly to detach it without damaging the stem or branch."
msgstr ""
"Tourner légèrement le fruit pour le détacher sans abîmer le pédoncule ou "
"la branche."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:297
msgid "Avoid pulling on fragile twigs."
msgstr "Éviter de tirer sur les rameaux fragiles."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:298
msgid "Prioritize ripe fruit only; several passes may be needed."
msgstr "Prioriser les fruits mûrs uniquement (plusieurs passages nécessaires)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:300
msgid "For larger trees:"
msgstr "Pour certains arbres plus grands :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:301
msgid ""
"Use a safe step ladder or suitable tools, such as telescopic picking "
"poles, if available."
msgstr ""
"Utiliser un escabeau sécuritaire ou des outils adaptés si disponibles "
"(perches télescopiques)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:302
msgid ""
"Very gently shake branches to drop ripe fruit onto a tarp suspended "
"beneath the branch."
msgstr ""
"Secouage très doux des branches pour faire tomber des fruits mûrs dans "
"une bâche suspendue sous la branche."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:307
msgid "Fully ripe fruit"
msgstr "Fruits bien mûrs"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:308
msgid "Fruit that is firm but slightly yielding"
msgstr "Fruits fermes mais souples"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:309
msgid "Intact fruit without cracks"
msgstr "Fruits intacts sans fissures"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:312
msgid "Green or unripe fruit"
msgstr "Fruits verts ou immatures"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:314
msgid "Soft or fermented fruit"
msgstr "Fruits mous ou fermentés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:315
msgid "Fruit with visible mould or larvae"
msgstr "Fruits présentant moisissures ou larves visibles"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:319
msgid "Plums are moderately fragile but become sensitive to crushing once ripe."
msgstr ""
"Les prunes sont modérément fragiles mais sensibles à l’écrasement une "
"fois mûres."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:323
msgid "Avoid piling; store in limited layers"
msgstr "Éviter d’empiler les fruits et les entreposer en couches limitées"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:324
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:404
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:552
msgid "Prompt refrigeration"
msgstr "Réfrigération rapide"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:328
msgid "High stacks of fruit"
msgstr "Empilement élevé"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:333
msgid "Prompt processing is recommended for surplus fruit."
msgstr "Transformation rapide recommandée pour surplus."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:336
msgid "Plums are popular but have a relatively short storage life."
msgstr "Fruits appréciés mais à durée de vie relativement courte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:337
msgid "Distribute them quickly while they are fresh."
msgstr "Distribution rapide recommandée pendant qu’elles sont fraîches."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:338
msgid "They are well suited to group processing during peak production."
msgstr "Très adaptés à la transformation collective lors des pics de production."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:339
msgid "They are sensitive to excessive handling."
msgstr "Sensibles à la manipulation excessive."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:340
msgid "Plums do not ripen after picking."
msgstr "Elles ne mûrissent pas après la cueillette."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:342
msgid "Pears"
msgstr "Poires"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:346
msgid ""
"In Montréal, pears are generally harvested from late August to October, "
"depending on the cultivar. Many varieties grow in urban areas. Maturity "
"varies considerably between trees and extends over several weeks."
msgstr ""
"À Montréal, les poires sont généralement récoltées de la mi-août à la mi-"
"octobre, selon les cultivars. Il existe beaucoup de variétés en milieu "
"urbain. La maturité varie fortement selon les arbres et s’étale sur "
"plusieurs semaines."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:350
msgid ""
"Pears should ideally be harvested **before they are fully ripe**, as they"
" ripen after harvest."
msgstr ""
"⚠️ Les poires se récoltent idéalement **avant maturité complète** "
"(maturation en post-récolte)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:353
msgid "The fruit is firm but detaches easily when lifted slightly."
msgstr "Fruit ferme mais qui se détache facilement quand légèrement soulevé."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:354
msgid ""
"The background colour is beginning to turn yellow or change (depending on"
" the cultivar)."
msgstr "Couleur de base qui commence à jaunir ou virer (selon cultivar)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:355
msgid "The flesh is still firm, not soft on the tree."
msgstr "Grain encore ferme (pas mou sur l’arbre)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:356
msgid "The fruit has reached its full size."
msgstr "Calibre maximum atteint."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:359
msgid "Fruit that is very hard and green and has not yet reached its full size."
msgstr "Fruits très durs et verts et pas encore ayant atteint leur plein gabarit."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:361
msgid ""
"Key field test: Lift the fruit slightly. If it detaches without force, it"
" is ready."
msgstr ""
"Test terrain clé : soulever légèrement le fruit → s’il se détache sans "
"forcer, il est prêt."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:364
msgid ""
"There is considerable variation between cultivars in texture, sweetness, "
"and maturity."
msgstr "Très forte variabilité entre cultivars (texture, douceur, maturité)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:365
msgid "Many urban pear trees are older or unidentified varieties."
msgstr "Beaucoup de poiriers urbains sont semi-anciens ou non identifiés."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:366
msgid ""
"Fruit does not ripen properly on the tree, so harvesting at the right "
"time is important."
msgstr ""
"Les fruits ne mûrissent pas correctement sur l’arbre → importance du bon "
"timing de récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:367
msgid "Some varieties are very prone to dropping prematurely."
msgstr "Certaines variétés sont très sensibles à la chute prématurée."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:368
msgid ""
"Production is often abundant but concentrated in a short window for each "
"tree."
msgstr ""
"Production souvent abondante mais concentrée sur une courte fenêtre par "
"arbre."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:369
msgid "Pear trees often show biennial bearing."
msgstr "Les poiriers ont souvent une production bisannuelle."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:373
msgid ""
"Pears can be picked in the same way as apples (see the section above), "
"but remember that they should be harvested before they are fully ripe. "
"This can sometimes make picking a little more difficult. Take extra care "
"not to pull the fruit, so you do not damage the spur."
msgstr ""
"Les poires peuvent être cueillies comme des pommes (voir la section ci-"
"dessus) mais souvenez- vous qu’elles doivent être cueillies avant d’être "
"complètement mûres, alors parfois les cueillir peut s’avérer un peu plus "
"difficile. Pendant que vous cueillez les poires, redoublez d’attention à "
"ne pas tirer le fruit afin de ne pas endommager la branche!"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:376
msgid "Lift and twist slightly to detach the fruit; do not pull."
msgstr "Soulever et tourner légèrement pour détacher le fruit (ne pas tirer)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:377
msgid "Avoid impacts, as pears are very susceptible to bruising."
msgstr "Éviter les chocs (poire = très sensible aux bleus)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:378
msgid "Prioritize accessible fruit and make several passes."
msgstr "Prioriser les fruits accessibles en plusieurs passages."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:380
msgid "For taller trees:"
msgstr "Pour les arbres plus hauts :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:381
msgid "Use a safe step ladder or telescopic picking poles."
msgstr "Utiliser un escabeau sécuritaire ou des perches télescopiques."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:382
msgid ""
"Shaking branches is not recommended because it can cause fruit to fall, "
"injure people, and damage the tree. Only do this if it is the only "
"practical way to harvest the fruit and you have a safe way to catch the "
"falling fruit in a tarp. In that case, the fruit is more likely to be "
"damaged and may be better suited to processing."
msgstr ""
"Le secouage des branches n’est pas recommandé (chute + blessures + "
"dégâts) sauf s’il est la seule moyenne de cueillir les fruits et que vous"
" avez une manière sécuritaire d’attraper les fruits tombants dans une "
"bâche. Dans ce cas la les fruits risquent plus de s'abimer et d'être "
"plutôt destinées à la transformation"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:387
msgid "Firm, intact fruit"
msgstr "Fruits fermes et intacts"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:388
msgid "Fruit without bruises or punctures"
msgstr "Fruits sans chocs ni perforations"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:389
msgid "Clean fruit with intact skin"
msgstr "Fruits propres, peau intacte"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:392
msgid "Fruit that is soft on the tree (too far advanced)"
msgstr "Fruits mous sur l’arbre (trop avancés)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:393
msgid "Fallen and damaged fruit"
msgstr "Fruits tombés et abîmés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:394
msgid "Fruit with bruises, punctures, or mould"
msgstr "Fruits avec coups, perforations ou moisissure"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:395
msgid "Very green, unripe fruit"
msgstr "Fruits très verts non mûrs"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:398
msgid "Pears are **very sensitive to impacts**, even when they seem firm."
msgstr ""
"Les poires sont **très sensibles aux chocs**, même si elles semblent "
"fermes."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:401
msgid ""
"Shallow, rigid containers. Bags may be acceptable if the fruit is handled"
" gently"
msgstr ""
"Contenants rigides peu profonds, mais des sacs pourraient être "
"acceptables si manipulé doucement"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:402
msgid "Ideally, a single layer"
msgstr "Une seule couche idéalement"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:403
#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:551
msgid "Minimal handling"
msgstr "Manipulation minimale"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:406
msgid "**Important characteristic:**"
msgstr "**Particularité importante :**"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:408
msgid ""
"Pears ripen after harvest (over a few days at room temperature or under "
"controlled conditions). Their texture deteriorates quickly if they ripen "
"on the tree."
msgstr ""
"Les poires mûrissent après la récolte (en quelques jours à température "
"ambiante ou contrôlée). Leur texture se dégrade rapidement si elles "
"mûrissent sur l’arbre."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:411
msgid ""
"Pears are often harvested while firm, so recipients may need an "
"explanation."
msgstr ""
"Récolte souvent faite à un stade ferme → nécessite parfois explication de"
" mûrissement auprès des bénéficiaires."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:412
msgid "They can keep very well if harvested correctly."
msgstr "Très bonne conservation si récoltées correctement."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:413
msgid "They are ideal for gradual distribution because ripening can be staggered."
msgstr "Idéales pour distribution progressive (maturation échelonnée)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:414
msgid ""
"Take care during transport: damage from impacts may not be visible at "
"first but can lead to rapid deterioration."
msgstr "Attention aux chocs en transport (dégradation rapide invisible au début)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:416
msgid "Saskatoon berries (serviceberries)"
msgstr "Amélanches"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:419
msgid ""
"Saskatoon berries are generally the first tree fruits to ripen during the"
" summer in Montréal. Harvest usually takes place between late June and "
"early July."
msgstr ""
"Les amélanches sont généralement les premiers fruits arboricoles à "
"arriver à maturité dans la saison estivale à Montréal. La récolte a "
"habituellement lieu entre la fin juin et le début juillet."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:421
msgid ""
"The optimal harvest window is often short and may vary with the weather. "
"During hot, dry periods, fruit can ripen very quickly and may even begin "
"to dry out on the tree if harvesting is delayed."
msgstr ""
"La fenêtre optimale de récolte est souvent courte et peut varier selon "
"les conditions météorologiques. Lors des périodes chaudes et sèches, les "
"fruits peuvent mûrir très rapidement et même commencer à se dessécher sur"
" l’arbre si la récolte tarde."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:425
msgid "Purple or dark violet fruit"
msgstr "Fruits mauves ou violet foncé"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:426
msgid "Fruit that is slightly soft"
msgstr "Fruits légèrement tendres"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:427
msgid "Sweet, fragrant flavour"
msgstr "Saveur sucrée et parfumée"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:431
msgid "Red or pink fruit"
msgstr "Fruits rouges ou rosés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:432
msgid "Firm fruit that is not very sweet"
msgstr "Fruits fermes et peu sucrés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:434
msgid ""
"Since not all fruit on the same tree necessarily ripens at the same time,"
" it can be helpful to make several passes during the harvest period."
msgstr ""
"Puisque tous les fruits d’un même arbre ne mûrissent pas nécessairement "
"en même temps, il peut être avantageux d’effectuer plusieurs passages "
"durant la période de récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:437
msgid ""
"Several species and varieties of serviceberry grow in Montréal. They "
"generally grow as small trees, shrubs, or suckering trees (sometimes "
"trained to have a single trunk). Fruit size, flavour, texture, and "
"productivity can vary from one tree to another."
msgstr ""
"Il existe plusieurs espèces et variétés d’amélanchiers à Montréal. Ils "
"poussent généralement en forme d'arbrisseaux, arbustes, ou arbre "
"drageonnant (parfois dressé pour avoir qu’un seul tronc). Les fruits "
"peuvent varier en taille, en saveur, en texture et en productivité selon "
"les arbres."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:439
msgid ""
"Birds are particularly fond of serviceberries and can consume a large "
"part of the crop within just a few days. Regularly monitoring trees as "
"the fruit approaches maturity is therefore recommended."
msgstr ""
"Les amélanches sont particulièrement appréciées par les oiseaux, qui "
"peuvent consommer une grande partie de la récolte en quelques jours "
"seulement. Une surveillance régulière des arbres est donc recommandée à "
"l’approche de la maturité."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:441
msgid "These small fruits are delicate and have a short storage life after picking."
msgstr ""
"Ces petits fruits sont délicats et ont une courte durée de conservation "
"après la récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:444
msgid "Pick serviceberries gently by hand to avoid crushing them."
msgstr ""
"Cueillir les amélanches délicatement à la main afin d’éviter de les "
"écraser."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:445
msgid "Harvest only ripe fruit."
msgstr "Récolter uniquement les fruits mûrs."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:446
msgid "Handle fruit carefully to preserve its quality."
msgstr "Manipuler les fruits avec soin pour préserver leur qualité."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:447
msgid "Avoid pulling excessively on branches."
msgstr "Éviter de tirer excessivement sur les branches."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:448
msgid ""
"When possible, make several successive harvests rather than one early "
"harvest."
msgstr ""
"Lorsque possible, effectuer plusieurs récoltes successives plutôt qu’une "
"seule récolte hâtive."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:450
msgid ""
"Serviceberries are an important food source for many urban bird and "
"small-mammal species. When quantities allow, it is recommended to leave "
"some of the harvest for wildlife."
msgstr ""
"Les amélanches constituent une source de nourriture importante pour "
"plusieurs espèces d’oiseaux et de petits mammifères urbains. Il est "
"recommandé de laisser une partie de la récolte à la faune lorsque les "
"quantités le permettent."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:453
msgid ""
"There is generally little need for sorting when fruit is picked directly "
"from the tree."
msgstr ""
"Le besoin de tri est généralement faible lorsque les fruits sont cueillis"
" directement sur l’arbre."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:456
msgid "Ripe, clean, well-formed fruit"
msgstr "Fruits mûrs, propres et bien formés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:459
msgid "Dried-out fruit"
msgstr "Fruits desséchés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:460
msgid "Damaged or crushed fruit"
msgstr "Fruits abîmés ou écrasés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:461
msgid "Fruit showing signs of mould"
msgstr "Fruits présentant des signes de moisissure"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:462
msgid "Fruit with significant abnormalities"
msgstr "Fruits présentant des anomalies importantes"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:464
msgid "It is preferable to leave inedible fruit on the tree rather than pick it."
msgstr ""
"Il est préférable de laisser les fruits non comestibles directement sur "
"l’arbre plutôt que de les récolter."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:467
msgid "Serviceberries are easily crushed and must be transported carefully."
msgstr ""
"Les amélanches s’écrasent facilement et doivent être transportées avec "
"précaution."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:469
msgid "Recommended containers"
msgstr "Contenants recommandés :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:470
msgid "Small, shallow, rigid containers"
msgstr "Petites barquettes rigides peu profondes"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:471
msgid "Reused containers for strawberries, raspberries, or blueberries"
msgstr "Contenants réutilisés pour les fraises, framboises ou bleuets"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:478
msgid "After harvesting:"
msgstr "Après la récolte :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:479
msgid "Keep fruit in the shade as much as possible."
msgstr "Garder les fruits à l’ombre autant que possible."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:480
msgid "Refrigerate promptly."
msgstr "Réfrigérer rapidement."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:481
msgid "Eat or distribute within the following few days."
msgstr "Consommer ou distribuer dans les jours suivants."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:482
msgid "Fruit can also be frozen for later use."
msgstr ""
"Les fruits peuvent également être congelés pour une utilisation "
"ultérieure."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:485
msgid ""
"Because they are fragile and have a short storage life, serviceberries "
"should ideally be redistributed soon after harvesting."
msgstr ""
"En raison de leur fragilité et de leur courte durée de conservation, les "
"amélanches devraient idéalement être redistribuées rapidement après la "
"récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:487
msgid ""
"Pay particular attention to packaging and transport to avoid crushing the"
" fruit."
msgstr ""
"Une attention particulière doit être portée au conditionnement et au "
"transport afin d’éviter l’écrasement des fruits."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:489
msgid "When possible, aim to distribute them within 24–48 hours of picking."
msgstr ""
"Lorsque possible, privilégier une distribution dans les 24 à 48 heures "
"suivant la cueillette."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:492
msgid "Grapes"
msgstr "Raisins"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:495
msgid ""
"In Montréal, grapes generally ripen between late August and October, "
"depending on the cultivar and exposure."
msgstr ""
"À Montréal, les raisins arrivent généralement à maturité entre la fin "
"août et octobre, selon les cultivars et l’exposition."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:497
msgid ""
"The most common varieties in urban areas are hardy hybrids (often derived"
" from Vitis labrusca), which are more cold-resistant than classic Vitis "
"vinifera grape varieties. Riverbank grape (Vitis riparia) is a wild, "
"native species in Québec, but its small fruits are generally more "
"appealing to wildlife than to people."
msgstr ""
"Les variétés les plus fréquentes en milieu urbain sont des hybrides "
"rustiques (souvent issus de Vitis labrusca), plus résistants au froid que"
" les cépages classiques de Vitis vinifera. La vigne des rivages(Vitis "
"riparia) est une espèce indigene et sauvage au Québec, mais dont les "
"petits fruits sont davantage appréciés par la faune que par les humains."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:499
msgid "Ripening progresses over time and can vary on the same vine."
msgstr "La maturation est progressive et peut varier sur un même plant."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:502
msgid ""
"Grapes should be harvested when fully ripe, as they do not continue to "
"ripen after picking."
msgstr ""
"Les raisins doivent être récoltés à pleine maturité, car ils ne "
"continuent pas à mûrir après la cueillette."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:504
msgid "Ready to pick:"
msgstr "Prêtes à cueillir :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:505
msgid ""
"Uniform colour according to the cultivar (golden green, red, or dark "
"purple)"
msgstr "Couleur uniforme selon le cultivar (vert doré, rouge, violet foncé)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:506
msgid "Berries that are yielding but still firm"
msgstr "Baies souples mais encore fermes"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:507
msgid "A well-developed sweet flavour, with less acidity"
msgstr "Goût sucré bien développé (moins acide)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:508
msgid "Grapes that detach easily from the cluster stem"
msgstr "Raisins qui se détachent facilement de la rafle"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:510
msgid "Leave on the vine:"
msgstr "À laisser sur la vigne :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:511
msgid "Green or acidic berries"
msgstr "Baies vertes ou acides"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:512
msgid "Very firm, small fruit"
msgstr "Fruits très fermes et petits"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:513
msgid "Clusters with uneven colour (incomplete ripening)"
msgstr "Grappes encore hétérogènes (maturation incomplète)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:516
msgid "Ripening is often uneven within a single cluster."
msgstr "Maturation souvent inégale dans une même grappe."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:517
msgid ""
"There is considerable variation between cultivars in acidity, size, and "
"skin thickness."
msgstr "Forte variabilité entre cultivars (acidité, taille, peau épaisse ou fine)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:518
msgid ""
"Some urban vines produce very large crops, but production varies from "
"year to year."
msgstr ""
"Certaines vignes urbaines produisent énormément mais de façon irrégulière"
" selon les années."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:519
msgid "Birds may consume a large part of the crop once the grapes ripen."
msgstr ""
"Les oiseaux peuvent consommer une grande partie de la récolte une fois la"
" maturité atteinte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:520
msgid "Clusters can dry out or deteriorate quickly at the end of the season."
msgstr "Les grappes peuvent sécher ou se dégrader rapidement en fin de saison."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:523
msgid "By hand: Cut clusters using clean pruning shears or scissors."
msgstr "À la main : Coupez les grappes à l’aide d’un sécateur ou de ciseaux."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:524
msgid "Cut the entire cluster with clean scissors or pruning shears."
msgstr "Couper la grappe entière avec des ciseaux ou sécateur propre."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:525
msgid "Handle gently to avoid crushing the berries."
msgstr "Manipuler délicatement pour éviter d’écraser les baies."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:526
msgid "Do not pull on clusters, as this can damage the vine."
msgstr "Éviter de tirer sur les grappes (risque d’endommager le plant)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:527
msgid ""
"Prioritize fully ripe clusters and avoid mixing fruit at very different "
"stages of maturity."
msgstr ""
"Prioriser les grappes entièrement mûres (éviter de mélanger trop de "
"stades)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:529
msgid "For tall vines:"
msgstr "Pour les vignes hautes :"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:530
msgid "Use a secure step ladder."
msgstr "Utiliser escabeau sécurisé."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:531
msgid "Do not pull on the branches, which are fragile and flexible."
msgstr "Ne pas tirer les branches (fragiles et flexibles)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:535
msgid "Healthy, intact clusters"
msgstr "Grappes saines et complètes"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:536
msgid "Firm berries without cracks"
msgstr "Baies fermes, sans fissures"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:537
msgid "Well-coloured, sweet grapes"
msgstr "Raisins bien colorés et sucrés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:540
msgid "Soft or split berries"
msgstr "Baies molles ou éclatées"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:541
msgid "Clusters with visible mould (advanced Botrytis)"
msgstr "Grappes avec moisissure visible (Botrytis avancé)"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:542
msgid "Fermented or badly damaged fruit"
msgstr "Fruits fermentés ou très abîmés"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:543
msgid "Partially dried-out or deteriorated clusters"
msgstr "Grappes partiellement sèches ou dégradées"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:546
msgid "Grapes are susceptible to crushing and rapid fermentation."
msgstr "Les raisins sont sensibles à l’écrasement et à la fermentation rapide."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:549
msgid "Small, rigid containers"
msgstr "Petits contenants rigides"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:550
msgid "Avoid thick layers"
msgstr "Éviter les couches épaisses"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:556
msgid "Prompt consumption is recommended after harvesting."
msgstr "Consommation rapide recommandée après récolte."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:557
msgid "Freezing is possible for culinary use."
msgstr "Congélation possible (usage culinaire)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:559
msgid "Storage"
msgstr "Entreposage"

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:561
msgid ""
"At Santropol Roulant, all fruits except apples can be put in the walk-in "
"fridge in the basement of the building (a.k.a. cold room, cold storage). "
"Apples can be put on the Fruits Défendus shelf unless they are in danger "
"of rotting. Please don't place containers on the floor of the walk-in "
"fridge."
msgstr ""
"Au Santropol Roulant, tous les fruits sauf les pommes peuvent être mis "
"dans le réfrigérateur dans le sous-sol. Les pommes peuvent être mises "
"dans l’étagère des Fruits Défendus sauf si elles sont en danger de "
"pourrir. Svp, ne déposez pas les conteneurs sur le sol du réfrigérateur."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:563
msgid ""
"\"Soft\" fruits (cherries, Saskatoon berries, plums, grapes) should be "
"stored in a way where they do not get crushed under their own weight. "
"Therefore, use small bags and try not to pile the bags on top of each "
"other. If you can, we recommend using recyclable plastic produce "
"containers (rigid packaging used for selling mixed greens, cherry "
"tomatoes, strawberries, etc.) to transport and store soft fruit. Wooden "
"boxes used to sell clementines can also be used for this."
msgstr ""
"Les fruits « mous » (cerises, amélanches, prunes et raisins) doivent être"
" entreposés à un endroit où ils ne sont pas écrasés par d’autres fruits "
"plus lourds. Vous pouvez utiliser de petits sacs en essayant de ne pas "
"remplir le sac en entier et de ne pas les entasser les uns sur les "
"autres. Nous vous recommandons d’utiliser des contenants réutilisables en"
" plastique (comme des emballages utilisés pour contenir divers légumes, "
"barquettes de fraises, tomates, etc.) pour transporter et entreposer les "
"fruits mous. Des cartons en bois utilisés habituellement pour les "
"clémentines peuvent également être utilisés."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:565
msgid ""
"Pears must be stored in a space where the temperature is close to 0 ° C; "
"otherwise they will continue to ripen. Pears stored at room temperature "
"will mature quickly and must be eaten a few days after picking. If unripe"
" pears are stored in the cold, they can be stacked without a problem. "
"However, if they are kept at room temperature, they should not be packed "
"too tightly."
msgstr ""
"Il convient d’entreposer les poires dans un espace dont la température "
"avoisine les 0°C, sinon elles continueront à mûrir. Les poires "
"entreposées à la température ambiante mûriront assez vite et pourront "
"être mangées quelques jours après la cueillette. Si vous entreposez les "
"poires non-mûres au froid, vous pouvez les mettre l’une par-dessus "
"l’autre sans problème, par contre, si elles sont à la température de la "
"salle, il ne faut pas qu’elles soient trop compactées."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:567
msgid "In summary:"
msgstr "En résumé : "

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:568
msgid ""
"Always sterilize harvesting tools (picking poles, bins, etc.) between "
"harvests to avoid spreading tree diseases from one tree to another."
msgstr ""
"Toujours stériliser les outils de cueillette (perches, bacs, etc.) entre "
"les cueillettes pour ne pas propager les maladies d’un arbre à l’autre."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:569
msgid ""
"Make sure you always choose a beneficiary organisation to which you can "
"donate the fruit, depending on its quality and quantity. It is best if "
"their activities are well suited to the type of fruit you are donating "
"(for example, processing organisations for soft fruit or small "
"quantities, or emergency aid organisations for beautiful, perfect fruit)."
msgstr ""
"Assurez-vous de toujours choisir un organisme bénéficiaire auquel donner "
"les fruits, selon leur qualité et leur quantité. Il est bien que leurs "
"activités soient bien adaptées au type de fruits que vous donnez (par "
"exemple, organismes de transformation pour des petits fruits ou petites "
"quantités, ou bien organismes de dépannage pour des beaux fruits "
"parfaits)."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:570
msgid "Please follow the picking guidelines set out in this guide."
msgstr "Respectez les consignes de cueillette décrites dans ce guide."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:571
msgid ""
"Never attempt to pick fruit from high branches, dangerous branches or "
"branches near power lines; the safety of the pickers must always be the "
"top priority. Even if the owner asks you to pick all the fruit from their"
" tree, you must explain to them that we only pick fruit that can be "
"reached safely."
msgstr ""
"Ne tentez jamais de cueillir des fruits disposés dans des branches "
"hautes, dangereuses ou près des fils électriques, il faut toujours "
"prioriser la sécurité des cueilleurs avant tout. Même si le ou la "
"propriétaire vous demande de tout cueillir les fruits de son arbre, il "
"est nécessaire que vous l’expliquez qu’on ne cueille que les fruits "
"accessibles en toute sécurité."

#: ../../docs/source/harvest-guide/how-to-harvest.md:572
msgid "Please give your fruit as soon as possible directly to the recipient."
msgstr "Donnez vos fruits le plus rapidement possible directement au bénéficiaire."